# Blog illustration guidelines

Vince the Validator is the publication mascot. Invent a **new** scene for each post that literalizes that article's idea. Exercise creative judgment. Do not clone prior compositions.

## Canonical Vince

- White humanoid robot; dark visor with **glowing cyan circuit-face** (short horizontal line eyes, faint traces — not round cartoon eyes)
- **Bright red fedora**, black ribbon band
- Charcoal waistcoat over dark turtleneck; white articulated arms
- Cyan **AI** badge; cyan sparkline on the pocket
- Role: validator / conductor / auditor — never a generic stock robot

Reference: `assets/images/thinkinginsidethebox.ai_logo_closeup.png`

## Palette and style

- Dark navy/black grounds; electric **cyan/teal** for digital elements; **red** reserved for the fedora and one narrative accent
- Occasional warm amber sidelight for cinematic posts
- Cinematic 3D digital illustration; tech-professional with a touch of whimsy
- Sparse graphic labels only. No walls of fake UI copy.

## Creative judgment (required)

- The editorial "box" is philosophy, **not** a mandatory cube. Use a cube only when it earns the metaphor.
- Do not reuse: glowing cube default, archive/holographic binders, stacking persona blocks, SPEC HUD over-the-shoulder, HITL flowchart, over-harnessed hallway.
- Guest posts (`author` other than the host) may omit Vince (`guest_technical_corporate`).
- Host posts should feature Vince as the focal character.

## OG image spec

- Exactly **1200 × 627 px** PNG at `assets/images/og/{post-slug}.png`
- Register the file in `_data/og-images.yml` and set post front matter `image:`
- Landscape LinkedIn header: Vince left-of-center, narrative space to the right
